<BaseLayout description="Isaac Daroch: PhD student exploring adaptive intelligence, world representations and autonomous agents. Inspect transparent experiments, publications and scientific notes."><Hero/><Research/><Story/><AgentDemo/><Publications/><Projects/>
<section class="section journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey-title"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">05 / A RESEARCH JOURNEY</p><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="journey-title" class="reveal">Engineering systems.<br/><em>Understanding intelligence.</em></h2><div><p>From applied software and data science to research questions about learning, representation and autonomous behavior.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Read my background ↗</a></div></div><div class="journey-line"><article class="reveal"><span class="mono">FOUNDATION</span><h3>Computer engineering</h3><p>Software, data and the discipline of building systems whose behavior can be inspected.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span class="mono">EXPLORATION</span><h3>International experience</h3><p>Study experience at TU Ilmenau through DAAD, and postgraduate training in computer engineering.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span class="mono">DIRECTION</span><h3>Doctoral research</h3><p>Advanced Systems Engineering at Universidad Andrés Bello, with interests in AI and adaptive agents.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="vision" class="section vision-section"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">06 / THE LONG-TERM VISION</p><h2 class="reveal">Intelligent beings.<br/>Persistent worlds.<br/><em>New ways to experience.</em></h2><div class="vision-copy"><p>My long-term ambition is to explore digital environments inhabited by artificial agents that can learn and adapt—and immersive ways for people to interact with those worlds.</p><p class="muted">This is a direction of exploration, not a claim that consciousness, digital life or fully immersive virtual reality has already been achieved.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Follow the research notebook ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">07 / SCIENCE IN THE OPEN</p><div class="section-heading"><h2 class="reveal">Make the reasoning<br/><em>visible.</em></h2><div><p>Technical notes, teaching activities and explanations of what an experiment actually shows. Communication should make the limits as clear as the idea.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-ghost" href="/research/">Read the notebook ↗</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/teaching/">Explore teaching ↗</a></div></div></div></div></section><Contact/></BaseLayout>
